e-physical-security walkthrough log — 2026-10-10
Worked-case lesson: no command line by design (brief §6).
The "run" is the physical-security operations review + operations calendar
authored and self-reviewed in-session against the SP 800-53 Rev. 5 Physical and
Environmental Protection (PE) family control areas.

Scope: fictional Kestrel Components HQ (continued from e-media-protection):
engineering, prototype lab, server room with design files.
Artifacts authored (all fictional, labeled):
  - 5 review areas with findings → decisions: guards (post orders, randomized
    patrols, quarterly tailgating test); badges (same-day leaver deactivation
    tied to HR checklist, quarterly zone review, visitor escort rules);
    mantrap/doors (duress + power-failure + piggybacking procedure; prop alarm
    to guard's radio); CCTV (rationalized placement with overlap, 90-day
    retention on access-controlled storage, weekly sample review);
    environmental (generator load test quarterly, water sensor → monitored SOC
    channel, temperature alerts re-routed, clean-agent verified, drill dated).
  - Operations calendar: daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly/annual items, every
    item with an owner.

